1. Introduction
1.1 Purpose of this Document
This comprehensive user manual serves as your primary instructional guide for operating the Voucher Posting & Authorization System. It is purposefully designed to assist all designated stakeholders—including Makers, Checkers, Approvers, and Administrators across various teams (such as SBI GLIF, TCS GLIF, and TCS IMPL)—in navigating the application accurately and efficiently.
This document outlines the end-to-end processes required for setting up Voucher IDs (VIDs), initiating manual or bulk postings, and executing multi-tiered authorization workflows. Whether you are submitting a new financial batch, auditing a pending request, or tracking a voucher's entire lifecycle, this guide provides clear, step-by-step instructions alongside our strict business rules to ensure compliance and accuracy.
1.2 System Overview & Key Features
The Voucher Posting & Authorization System is a secure, role-based financial application built to manage and validate critical ledger entries. It minimizes human error through strict system-level validations and ensures that only clean, verified data reaches the core ledger through a mandatory multistage approval process.
Key Features Include:
￼ Maker-Checker Security: A single user cannot both create and approve the same financial entry. This guarantees a secure separation of duties.
￼ Voucher IDs (VIDs): The system utilizes pre-approved VIDs (created by the SBI GLIF team) that act as strict templates. This ensures Makers only post transactions to approved categories and ledger combinations.
￼ Dual Entry Methods: The system supports both Manual Data Entry for quick adjustments and robust Bulk Excel Uploads for processing thousands of rows simultaneously.
￼ Real-Time Validation: The system actively intercepts errors by forcing exact Debit and Credit balancing across all Branch and Currency combinations before a batch can even be submitted.
￼ Flexible Execution Scheduling: Creators or Final Approvers can choose to post vouchers immediately, or schedule them to automatically execute at a specific time later in the day to avoid peak operational hours.
￼ Comprehensive Audit Trails: A detailed "View & Action" portal tracks every stage, timestamp, and user remark throughout the voucher's lifespan for full transparency.
